theory.intro:
Two vectors are **parallel** when one is a scalar multiple of the other, $\underset{\sim}{b}=k\underset{\sim}{a}$. They point the same way if $k>0$ and opposite ways if $k<0$. The same $k$ must work in every component.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.1]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw[-{Stealth},thick] (0,2.4)--(2,3.4) node[right]{$\underset{\sim}{a}$};
\draw[-{Stealth},thick,blue] (0,1.2)--(3,2.7) node[right]{$k\underset{\sim}{a}$ with $k>0$};
\draw[-{Stealth},thick,red] (0,0)--(-2.4,-1.2) node[left]{$k\underset{\sim}{a}$ with $k<0$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
